  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{宥|なだ}める.\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed when dealing with someone in an emotional state — crying, angry, or panicking. The subject is always trying to restore calm through words, gestures, or comfort.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {子供|こども}を{宥|なだ}める: to soothe a child\n- {怒|いか}りを{宥|なだ}める: to calm someone's anger\n- {泣|な}いている{人|ひと}を{宥|なだ}める: to comfort someone who is crying\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{落|お}ち{着|つ}かせる means \"to make someone calm down\" and is more neutral. {宥|なだ}める implies a gentler, more soothing approach, often with words of comfort. {慰|なぐさ}める (to console) focuses more on emotional comfort after loss or sadness, whereas {宥|なだ}める focuses on calming active distress.",
